 {"id":"README-12","status":"pending","priority":"P5","type":"task","title":"P5 — README Quickstart compile sample renders checks as indented code while the binary prints ```sh fences, under a 'pasted verbatim' promise","reasoning":"P5 — README Quickstart compile sample rendering drift (doc severity P5 by Bane ruling 2026-09-30).\n\nFINDING (audited tip 377baa0d93dfa020cc738ca4cd7527a5d5876bc8, README.md content sha256 c40222d1a0df7206bcd9c169970bd8a912b47ada8b16b48640727c6cb97494bd):\nREADME.md:27 promises 'Every command below was run and its output pasted verbatim'; README.md:103 calls the compile sample 'Abridged real output'. But the sample's Check 1 block at README.md:116-121 renders the command as a 4-space-indented line, while the binary prints every check command inside a ```sh fenced block (lore/runbook.py:128 prints '```sh'; fence present since 7cbdb70 2026-09-23, so the indented form never matched any revision's real output in the current sample shape).\n\nEXACT PROBES AND OUTPUTS (full transcripts frozen in the evidence directory):\n- uv run python -m lore compile --class gateway-drain-window --format md  (exit 0) prints:\n  '### Check 1 (read-only)' then a blank line, then the literal three-backtick 'sh' fence line, then logsey query \"SELECT message, ts FROM logs WHERE message LIKE '%drain 503%' AND ts >= now() - INTERVAL 30 MINUTE\", then the closing fence. (sweep.txt lines 79-84.)\n- README.md:116-118 in the same tree prints '### Check 1 (read-only)' then the SAME command indented four spaces with no fence lines. Healthy/Incident/Decision lines match live output; only the check-command rendering drifted.\n\nWHY P5: presentation fidelity of a pasted sample under an explicit verbatim promise; every claim inside the sample is otherwise accurate. Not a functional defect.\nNOT a sibling of: README-3 (audit bucket column), README-5 (show --evidence trail), README-6 (INSTALL unknown-class paste), README-7-R2 (INSTALL compile JSON signature), DOC-10-R2 (version claims) — no existing row owns this surface.\n\nFIX: in the README Quickstart compile sample (README.md:104-127), quote the checks the way the binary prints them (```sh fenced commands, matching lore/runbook.py:128) — or, if the outer four-backtick fence makes that awkward, drop the 'pasted verbatim' promise at README.md:27 and label the block 'abridged AND reformatted'. Either resolution may be picked by the fixer; do not silently claim verbatim over reformatted output.\nAUDIENCES: contributors / end-user readers diffing their own compile output against the README sample; the README's verbatim promise is the product's honesty law applied to itself.\nMECHANISM: sample-output rendering drifted while the paste around it stayed current; same class as README-6/README-7 (pasted output blocks not re-measured against the live renderer).\n\nACCEPTANCE (falsifiable):\n1. uv run python -m lore compile --class gateway-drain-window --format md | grep -A2 'Check 1' shows the command inside fence lines, and the README Quickstart compile sample renders checks the same way (no 4-space-indented bare command under '### Check 1').\n2. README.md:27 no longer promises 'pasted verbatim' unless every block it covers is byte-faithful (fencing included).\n3. The rest of the sweep holds: pytest 586 passed; ruff clean; readme-link-check local_missing=0 external_non_200=0; check-md-anchors broken=0.\n\nEVIDENCE ARTIFACT (frozen this sweep, sha256 84e0478d7734378690985a9628fafd5239ab6ad138e4dc33959559bf96af686f): docs/qa/evidence/run-README-12/README.md — plus full sweep transcripts docs/qa/evidence/run-README-12/sweep.txt (sha256 e6df324b4096370fbab22c6aa98cba976ef70d688dcddce2d365c44dbab03d85) and docs/qa/evidence/run-README-12/sweep-supp.txt (sha256 bb5f41e21ebd8c6a3165652b62bc530216f65f22fd7d7320ea5fb8ae42446744).\n\nch:trace row=README-12 spec=README.md#quickstart wave=none:serial-docs-tick test=none:no-arm-guards-sample-output-fidelity doc=README.md evidence=docs/qa/evidence/run-READM